Cell["\<\
At first, it\[CloseCurlyQuote]s easiest to read this from bottom to top. 
More broadly, the importance of this is that symbolic manipulation software \
like Mathematica in fact stores mathematical expressions as trees internally. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.972530877883337*^9, 3.972530920122566*^9}, {
   3.972534392364841*^9, 3.972534436907872*^9}, 3.9726986630962057`*^9, {
